<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">taunt</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">taunt</ansi> command launches a verbal assault against your
opponent, dealing <ansi fg="stat">conviction damage</ansi> instead of physical
damage. It attacks their will to fight rather than their body.

<ansi fg="yellow">Requirements:</ansi>

  - Must be in active combat
  - Cannot be used if special move cooldown is active

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">taunt</ansi>
  Hurl a scathing verbal attack at your current combat target

<ansi fg="yellow">Mechanics:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="stat">Hit Check:</ansi> Opposed roll
    - Attacker: Charisma + Rhetoric skill
    - Defender: Willpower + Rhetoric skill
  <ansi fg="stat">Damage:</ansi> Based on Charisma, Rhetoric rank, and target's
    conviction mitigation
  <ansi fg="stat">Damage Type:</ansi> Conviction (mental/social)
  <ansi fg="stat">Cooldown:</ansi> 5 rounds (shared with bash, trip, and kick)
  <ansi fg="stat">Skill:</ansi> Progresses Rhetoric

<ansi fg="yellow">Aggro Pull:</ansi>

  When a taunt lands against a creature that is fighting someone
  else, the creature is forced to turn its attention to you. This
  makes taunt a powerful tool for drawing enemies away from weaker
  allies and controlling the flow of battle.

  Aggro pull triggers on both normal hits and critical hits. It
  only applies to hostile creatures — taunting another player will
  not redirect their attacks.

As a target's conviction drains, their fighting spirit fades with it —
their attacks and defenses weaken steadily, the same way exhaustion
saps a fighter. Conviction recovers over time like health and stamina.

Armor with <ansi fg="stat">conviction mitigation</ansi> reduces taunt damage.
Items like willpower amulets or enchanted robes may provide
this protection.

